From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0580: ui_overlay_active_when_drawn: the UI overlay counts as shown only while something is drawn, so 04a0's fused gamma paint is made

Source: Ours (stream LOCK60 wave 2, F2f; finding by stream HDR). Validated in game: lk-fl4, lk-fl6, lk-val2
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: ReXApp always creates the AchievementToastDialog, so the ImGui drawer is registered all run and 04a0 refused the fused paint
  ('a UI overlay is shown'). Cvar ui_overlay_active_when_drawn (false; PC profile true): UIDrawer::DrewSomething /
  ImGuiDialog::HasVisibleContent (the toast: only while queued); conservative two-loop hysteresis and a wake counter for a dialog
  or toast that appears; the empty overlay composite is skipped. Swap group -0.18 ms (lk-fl4/6).
Bucket: REDO

0580-ui-overlay-active-when-drawn.patch (mcla-x86 LOCK60 wave 2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h b/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
index 7be49e0b..93677b51 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
@@ -48,6 +48,12 @@ class ImGuiDialog {
   // presents of its own.
   virtual bool RepaintsContinuously() const { return true; }
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0580): ui_overlay_active_when_drawn. Whether the dialog has something to show now or is about
+  // to (so the presenter can tell the drawer is registered with nothing on the screen). Called in the UI thread, after
+  // the dialog's Draw. A dialog that exists is shown, which is the default; one that stays registered while idle (the
+  // achievement toast, between toasts) says false while it is.
+  virtual bool HasVisibleContent() const { return true; }
+
  protected:
   ImGuiDialog(ImGuiDrawer* imgui_drawer);
 
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/imgui_drawer.h b/include/rex/ui/imgui_drawer.h
